IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- LAYER 1: ASSAULTS (the heading "Assaults",
-- sections 36 to 47).
--
-- What this part contains: special assaults on clergy, officers saving wreck, and
-- persons resisting apprehension (36 to 38); two summary offences on grain and seamen
-- (39, 40); the summary jurisdiction over common assault and battery (42), and the
-- certificate and the bar that follow it (44, 45); and assault occasioning actual
-- bodily harm (47).  Sections 41, 43 (text), 46 are rows of dots.  The text never
-- defines "assault", "battery" or "actual bodily harm"; each is a fact the person
-- states.
--
-- Sections 44 and 45 are not offences.  They give the person complained against a
-- claim to a certificate (section 44) and an immunity from further proceedings
-- (section 45); the correlative duty and disability sit on the justices and on the
-- party aggrieved.

§ `Assaults`

§§ `Section 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister in the discharge of his duties`

-- src:61 | 36 Obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister in the discharge of his duties.
-- src:62 | Whosoever shall, by threats or force, obstruct or prevent or endeavour to obstruct or prevent, any clergyman or other minister in or from celebrating divine service or otherwise officiating in any church, chapel, meeting house, or other place of divine worship, or in or from the performance of his duty in the lawful burial of the dead in any churchyard or other burial place, or shall strike or offer any violence to, or shall, upon any civil process, or under the pretence of executing any civil process, arrest any clergyman or other minister who is engaged in, or to the knowledge of the offender is about to engage in, any of the rites or duties in this section aforesaid, or who to the knowledge of the offender shall be going to perform the same or returning from the performance thereof, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable, at the discretion of the court, to be imprisoned for any term not exceeding two years, . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 36 (src:61-62)
-- Two kinds of act.  (A) By threats or force, obstructing or preventing, or endeavouring
-- to obstruct or prevent, a clergyman or other minister (1) in or from celebrating
-- divine service or otherwise officiating in a place of divine worship, or (2) in or
-- from the performance of their duty in the lawful burial of the dead in a churchyard
-- or other burial place.  (B) Striking or offering violence to, or arresting on civil
-- process (or under the pretence of it), a minister who (i) is engaged in any of those
-- rites or duties, or (ii) "to the knowledge of the offender is about to engage in"
-- them, or (iii) "to the knowledge of the offender shall be going to perform the same
-- or returning from the performance thereof".
-- FORK (see NOTES.md): "to the knowledge of the offender" is read as attaching to (ii)
-- and (iii) only; (i), a minister actually engaged, needs no knowledge.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 36` HAS
    `by threats or force obstructed or prevented, or endeavoured to obstruct or prevent, a clergyman or other minister in or from celebrating divine service or otherwise officiating in a place of divine worship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by threats or force obstructed or prevented, or endeavoured to obstruct or prevent, a clergyman or other minister in or from the performance of their duty in the lawful burial of the dead in a churchyard or other burial place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `struck or offered violence to a clergyman or other minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `arrested a clergyman or other minister, upon civil process or under the pretence of executing civil process` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the minister was engaged in those rites or duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the minister was about to engage in those rites or duties, to the knowledge of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the minister was going to perform those rites or duties or returning from performing them, to the knowledge of the person` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 36 (src:62)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 36`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister` c MEANS
        c's `by threats or force obstructed or prevented, or endeavoured to obstruct or prevent, a clergyman or other minister in or from celebrating divine service or otherwise officiating in a place of divine worship`
    OR  c's `by threats or force obstructed or prevented, or endeavoured to obstruct or prevent, a clergyman or other minister in or from the performance of their duty in the lawful burial of the dead in a churchyard or other burial place`
    OR  (    (   c's `struck or offered violence to a clergyman or other minister`
              OR c's `arrested a clergyman or other minister, upon civil process or under the pretence of executing civil process`)
         AND (   c's `the minister was engaged in those rites or duties`
              OR c's `the minister was about to engage in those rites or duties, to the knowledge of the person`
              OR c's `the minister was going to perform those rites or duties or returning from performing them, to the knowledge of the person`))

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 36 (src:62)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 36: what the text calls the offence` MEANS misdemeanor

-- "liable, at the discretion of the court, to be imprisoned for any term not exceeding
-- two years": 24 months.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 36 (src:62)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 36: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 24)

§§ `Section 37: assaulting a magistrate, &c. on account of his preserving wreck`

-- src:63 | 37 Assaulting a magistrate, &c. on account of his preserving wreck.
-- src:64 | Whosoever shall assault and strike or wound any magistrate, officer, or other person whatsoever lawfully authorized, in or on account of the exercise of his duty in or concerning the preservation of any vessel in distress, or of any vessel, goods, or effects wrecked, stranded, or cast on shore, or lying under water, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable . . . to be kept in penal servitude for any term not exceeding seven years . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 37 (src:63-64)
-- "assault and strike or wound": an assault, and a striking or a wounding.  The victim
-- is "any magistrate, officer, or other person whatsoever lawfully authorized", struck
-- or wounded "in or on account of the exercise of his duty in or concerning the
-- preservation of" a vessel in distress, or a vessel, goods or effects wrecked,
-- stranded, cast on shore or lying under water.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 37` HAS
    `assaulted and struck a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `assaulted and wounded a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was a magistrate, officer or other person lawfully authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was in or on account of the exercise of their duty in or concerning the preservation of a vessel in distress, or of a vessel, goods or effects wrecked, stranded, cast on shore or lying under water` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 37 (src:64)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 37`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37: assaulting a person preserving a vessel or wreck` c MEANS
        (   c's `assaulted and struck a person`
         OR c's `assaulted and wounded a person`)
    AND c's `the person was a magistrate, officer or other person lawfully authorized`
    AND c's `it was in or on account of the exercise of their duty in or concerning the preservation of a vessel in distress, or of a vessel, goods or effects wrecked, stranded, cast on shore or lying under water`

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 37 (src:64)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 37: what the text calls the offence` MEANS misdemeanor

-- "penal servitude for any term not exceeding seven years": 84 months.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 37 (src:64)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 37: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` (`for a term not exceeding` 84)

§§ `Section 38: assault with intent to commit felony, or on peace officers, &c.`

-- src:65 | 38 Assault with intent to commit felony, or on peace officers, &c.
-- src:66 | Whosoever . . . shall assault any person with intent to resist or prevent the lawful apprehension or detainer of himself or of any other person for any offence, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable, at the discretion of the court, to be imprisoned for any term not exceeding two years, . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 38 (src:65-66)
-- The text opens with ". . ." before "shall assault any person": words are missing,
-- and the section's own heading mentions "felony" and "peace officers" which the
-- remaining words do not.  The encoding takes what is left: an assault, with the
-- intent to resist or prevent the lawful apprehension or detainer of the person
-- assaulted or of any other person, for any offence.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 38` HAS
    `assaulted a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to resist or prevent the lawful apprehension or detainer of themselves for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to resist or prevent the lawful apprehension or detainer of another person for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 38 (src:66)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 38`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38: assault with intent to resist or prevent lawful apprehension` c MEANS
        c's `assaulted a person`
    AND (   c's `intended to resist or prevent the lawful apprehension or detainer of themselves for an offence`
         OR c's `intended to resist or prevent the lawful apprehension or detainer of another person for an offence`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 38 (src:66)
