§§ `Section 39: assaults with intent to obstruct the sale of grain, or its free passage`

-- src:67 | 39 Assaults with intent to obstruct the sale of grain, or its free passage.
-- src:68 | Whosoever shall beat, or use any violence or threat of violence to any person, with intent to deter or hinder him from buying, selling, or otherwise disposing of, or to compel him to buy, sell, or otherwise dispose of, any wheat or other grain, flour, meal, malt, or potatoes, in any market or other place, or shall beat or use any such violence or threat to any person having the care or charge of any wheat or other grain, flour, meal, malt, or potatoes, whilst on the way to or from any city, market town, or other place, with intent to stop the conveyance of the same, shall on conviction thereof before two justices of the peace be liable to be imprisoned . . . in the common gaol or house of correction for any term not exceeding three months: Provided, that no person who shall be punished for any such offence by virtue of this section shall be punished for the same offence by virtue of any other law whatsoever.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 39 (src:67-68)
-- Two limbs.  (1) Beating, or using violence or a threat of violence to, any person with
-- intent to deter or hinder them from buying, selling or otherwise disposing of, or to
-- compel them to buy, sell or otherwise dispose of, wheat or other grain, flour, meal,
-- malt or potatoes in any market or other place.  (2) Beating or using such violence or
-- threat to a person having the care or charge of such goods, whilst on the way to or
-- from a city, market town or other place, with intent to stop their conveyance.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 39` HAS
    `beat, or used violence or a threat of violence to, a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to deter or hinder them from buying, selling or otherwise disposing of, or to compel them to buy, sell or otherwise dispose of, wheat, other grain, flour, meal, malt or potatoes in a market or other place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person had the care or charge of wheat, other grain, flour, meal, malt or potatoes, whilst on the way to or from a city, market town or other place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to stop the conveyance of it` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 39 (src:68)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 39`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39: violence to obstruct the sale or conveyance of grain` c MEANS
        c's `beat, or used violence or a threat of violence to, a person`
    AND (   c's `intended to deter or hinder them from buying, selling or otherwise disposing of, or to compel them to buy, sell or otherwise dispose of, wheat, other grain, flour, meal, malt or potatoes in a market or other place`
         OR (    c's `the person had the care or charge of wheat, other grain, flour, meal, malt or potatoes, whilst on the way to or from a city, market town or other place`
             AND c's `intended to stop the conveyance of it`))

