§§ `Section 44: if the magistrates dismiss the complaint, they shall make out a certificate to that effect`

-- src:76 | 44 If the magistrates dismiss the complaint, they shall make out a certificate to that effect.
-- src:77 | If the justices, upon the hearing of any such case of assault or battery upon the merits, where the complaint was preferred by or on behalf of the party aggrieved, under either of the last two preceding sections, shall deem the offence not to be proved, or shall find the assault or battery to have been justified, or so trifling as not to merit any punishment, and shall accordingly dismiss the complaint, they shall forthwith make out a certificate . . . stating the fact of such dismissal, and shall deliver such certificate to the party against whom the complaint was preferred.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 44 (src:76-77)
-- "the last two preceding sections" are sections 42 and 43; section 43 is blank here.
-- The finding is the JUSTICES' (they "deem" or "find"), so it is taken as a fact about
-- the hearing, not for the person to state about themselves.  A duty of the justices,
-- and a claim of the person complained against.
DECLARE `Dismissal under section 44` HAS
    `a complaint was preferred by or on behalf of the party aggrieved under section 42 or 43` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the justices heard the case upon the merits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the justices deemed the offence not proved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the justices found the assault or battery justified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the justices found the assault or battery so trifling as not to merit any punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the justices dismissed the complaint` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 44 (src:77)
GIVEN d IS A `Dismissal under section 44`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44: a certificate of dismissal is owed to the person complained against` d MEANS
        d's `a complaint was preferred by or on behalf of the party aggrieved under section 42 or 43`
    AND d's `the justices heard the case upon the merits`
    AND (   d's `the justices deemed the offence not proved`
         OR d's `the justices found the assault or battery justified`
         OR d's `the justices found the assault or battery so trifling as not to merit any punishment`)
    AND d's `the justices dismissed the complaint`

-- "they shall forthwith make out a certificate . . . stating the fact of such
-- dismissal, and shall deliver such certificate to the party against whom the
-- complaint was preferred".  No number of days is stated.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 44 (src:77)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 44: when the certificate is due` MEANS "forthwith"

§§ `Section 45: certificate or conviction shall be a bar to any other proceedings`

-- src:78 | 45 Certificate or conviction shall be a bar to any other proceedings.
-- src:79 | If any person against whom any such complaint as in section 44 of this Act shall have been preferred by or on the behalf of the party aggrieved shall have obtained such certificate, or, having been convicted, shall have paid the whole amount adjudged to be paid, or shall have suffered the imprisonment . . . awarded, in every such case he shall be released from all further or other proceedings, civil or criminal, for the same cause.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 45 (src:78-79)
-- An immunity of the person complained against, and a disability of the party aggrieved
-- (and of anyone else who might bring "civil or criminal" proceedings "for the same
-- cause").  The three ways in are alternatives: obtaining the certificate; or, having
-- been convicted, paying the whole amount adjudged; or, having been convicted, having
-- suffered the imprisonment awarded.
DECLARE `Release under section 45` HAS
    `a complaint of the kind in section 44 was preferred by or on behalf of the party aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person obtained such a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person, having been convicted, paid the whole amount adjudged to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person, having been convicted, suffered the imprisonment awarded` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 45 (src:79)
GIVEN r IS A `Release under section 45`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45: the person is released from all further proceedings, civil or criminal, for the same cause` r MEANS
        r's `a complaint of the kind in section 44 was preferred by or on behalf of the party aggrieved`
    AND (   r's `the person obtained such a certificate`
         OR r's `the person, having been convicted, paid the whole amount adjudged to be paid`
         OR r's `the person, having been convicted, suffered the imprisonment awarded`)

